timeline.body:
How does this rewrite ever exit and do we continually append the alias filter on subsequent rewrites?

What do you think about adding this code to `doToQuery` instead of rewrite? It seems to me that the aliasFilter will be rewritten already and then when we call `doToQuery` we take the filter and append it to the list (not updating the query object, but instead adjusting the boolean query directly)

Like:
```
        BooleanQuery.Builder builder = new BooleanQuery.Builder();
        for (QueryBuilder query : this.filterQueries) {
            builder.add(query.toQuery(context), BooleanClause.Occur.FILTER);
        }
        if (searchExecutionContext.getAliasFilter() != null) {
            builder.add(searchExecutionContext.getAliasFilter().toQuery(context), BooleanClause.Occur.FILTER);
        }
        BooleanQuery booleanQuery = builder.build();
        Query filterQuery = booleanQuery.clauses().isEmpty() ? null : booleanQuery;

```

